# Accessibility

Accessibility is not a feature; it's the floor. We target **WCAG 2.2 AA** and follow the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices for interaction patterns. ShopStack Portal is a productivity tool — most users live in it for hours, and many depend on keyboard or assistive tech. Get this right and everyone benefits.

## 1. Use the right HTML element

A `<button>` is a `<button>`. A `<div>` with `onClick` is bait. Native elements come with focus, keyboard, role, and screen-reader semantics for free.

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG
<div className="btn" onClick={save}>Save</div>

// ✅ CORRECT
<button type="button" onClick={save}>Save</button>
```

If a button is inside a `<form>`, set `type="button"` unless it's the submit button — otherwise Enter inside any input triggers it.

## 2. Lean on Radix UI

We use Radix primitives (Dialog, Popover, Tabs, Select, Toast, Dropdown, etc.). They implement the WAI-ARIA pattern correctly — focus trapping, ESC handling, roving tabindex, ARIA labels. **Wrap Radix; don't replace it.**

When wrapping a Radix primitive with `cva`:

- Don't remove `aria-*` or `role` attributes Radix sets.
- Forward `ref` so consumers can manage focus.
- Spread `...rest` last so consumers can override classes.

## 3. Keyboard

Every interactive element must be reachable, operable, and visible via the keyboard.

- **Tab** moves between focusable elements in DOM order.
- **Enter** activates buttons, links, submits forms.
- **Space** activates buttons, toggles checkboxes.
- **Esc** closes modals, popovers, command palettes.
- **Arrow keys** move within a composite widget (menu, tabs, listbox, combobox) — Radix handles this.

Custom widgets must follow the matching WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices pattern; cite the pattern in a comment when implementing.

## 4. Focus management

- Never `outline: none` without a replacement. Use `:focus-visible` rings (Tailwind `focus-visible:ring-2`).
- When a modal opens, focus moves into it. When it closes, focus returns to the trigger. (Radix Dialog does this for you.)
- After a route change, move focus to the page's `<h1>` or a `role="main"` landmark.
- Hidden elements (`hidden`, `display:none`, `aria-hidden="true"`) must not be focusable. Don't use `tabIndex={-1}` to "fix" something; fix the underlying issue.

## 5. Labels

Every form control has an accessible name.

```tsx
// ✅ explicit
<label htmlFor="email">Email</label>
<input id="email" type="email" />

// ✅ via Radix Label
<Label.Root htmlFor="email">Email</Label.Root>
<input id="email" />

// ✅ aria-label when visual label is impractical (e.g. icon-only)
<button aria-label="Close" onClick={onClose}><X /></button>
```

Placeholder text is **not** a label. Floating labels must remain visible while the field has content.

## 6. Errors

Field errors are connected to the input with `aria-describedby` and announced with `role="alert"` (or `aria-live="polite"` for non-blocking warnings).

```tsx
<input id="email" aria-invalid={Boolean(errors.email)} aria-describedby="email-error" />
{errors.email && <p id="email-error" role="alert">{errors.email.message}</p>}
```

Errors must be visible (not solely indicated by color — also include icon or text).

## 7. Color and contrast

- Body text contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 against background (WCAG 2.2 AA).
- Large text (≥18pt or 14pt bold) ≥ 3:1.
- UI components and focus indicators ≥ 3:1.
- Never use color alone to convey state. Pair with text, icon, or pattern.

Tailwind tokens that pass: configure them in `tailwind.config` or the `@theme` block and reference by name. Don't hand-pick colors per component.

## 8. Motion

- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Wrap non-essential animations:

  ```css
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .animate-slide { animation: none; }
  }
  ```

- For `motion` (framer-motion successor), use `useReducedMotion()` and short-circuit animations.
- Avoid auto-playing media. If unavoidable, give users a control.

## 9. Images

- Every `<img>` has an `alt`. Decorative images get `alt=""`.
- Functional images (icon-only links/buttons) get the label on the parent control, not the image (and `alt=""`).
- SVG icons from `lucide-react` are `aria-hidden` by default; the surrounding control names the action.

## 10. Live regions

For non-blocking status updates (toasts, "Saved", search-result counts), use `aria-live="polite"`. `react-hot-toast` configures this. Don't roll your own.

`aria-live="assertive"` interrupts the user — reserve for true urgency (e.g. "Connection lost").

## 11. Headings

- Each page has exactly one `<h1>`.
- Heading levels don't skip (`h1` → `h3` is wrong). Use CSS to size, not heading level.
- Landmarks (`<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`) appear once at the top level. Multiple `<nav>` need `aria-label`.

## 12. Tables (`@tanstack/react-table`)

- Use `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tbody>`, `<th scope="col">`. Don't `<div>`-table unless you also implement the full `role="grid"` pattern.
- Sortable column headers expose `aria-sort="ascending" | "descending" | "none"`.
- Empty state has accessible text, not just an illustration.

## 13. Forms

- Group related inputs in `<fieldset>` with `<legend>`.
- `autocomplete` attributes set correctly (`email`, `new-password`, `current-password`, `street-address`, etc.) — improves both accessibility and security UX.
- Don't disable paste on password fields. It blocks password managers.

## 14. Modals and dialogs

- Use Radix Dialog (`role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, focus trap built in).
- Trigger element receives focus on close.
- Esc closes (Radix default — don't override).
- Background content gets `aria-hidden="true"` while modal is open (Radix default).

## 15. Skip link

The app shell renders a "Skip to main content" link as the first focusable element. It's visually hidden until focused. Target the `<main>` element by id.

## 16. Testing

- **Vitest** runs `@axe-core/react` on rendered components for key flows.
- **Playwright** runs `@axe-core/playwright` on every e2e test target page.
- New components must have at least one Testing Library test that finds them via `getByRole` / `getByLabelText`. If you can't, the component is inaccessible.

## Pre-merge checklist

- [ ] Every interactive element is reachable by Tab and operable by Enter/Space
- [ ] Visible focus indicator on every focusable element
- [ ] Every `<img>`, icon-only control, and form input has an accessible name
- [ ] Color contrast checked (use the DevTools Accessibility Inspector)
- [ ] No `outline: none` without a `:focus-visible` replacement
- [ ] `axe` clean on the changed pages

